IMPORT prelude

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 5), 2002 Revised Edition:
-- regulation 65(2) and (3) (the rest of regulation 65 is in sgta-i-rg5-radio.l4), Part IX (duties and general obligations,
-- regs 66 to 75) and Part X (regs 76, 77, 79 and 80; regulation 78 is in sgta-i-rg5-radio.l4).
-- Text: subjects/sg/telecommunications-radio-communication-regulations-2001/registers/source-bundle/TA1999-RG5.txt.
-- The Part IX duties are conditions of licences or duties on any person; regulation 78 makes a contravention of some of them an offence.

§ `Rg 5 regulation 65(2) and (3): the class licence's conditions and fee`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1096 | (2) A class licence shall be subject to the conditions specified in the Third Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1097 | (3) No fee is payable for a class licence.
@ref Rg 5 reg 65(2) and (3) (src:TA1999-RG5:1096-1097)
GIVEN `the Third Schedule's conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 65(2): the class licensee is within the class licence` MEANS
    `the Third Schedule's conditions are met`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 5 reg 65(3): the fee payable for a class licence in dollars` MEANS 0

§ `Rg 5 regulations 66 and 67: inspection`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1114 | 66. —(1) It is a condition of every licence that the licensee shall permit or ensure that
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1115 | permission is granted to an authorised officer, upon production of proof of identity, to
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1116 | enter any building, premises, compound or other place, vehicle, vessel or aircraft where
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1117 | any station or network is installed, or is being installed, to enable that officer to inspect,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1118 | examine or test any equipment comprised in the station or network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1119 | (2) Where the owner or user of a station or network requests the Authority to inspect,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1120 | for the second or subsequent time, any station or network licensed or to be licensed under
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1121 | these Regulations to verify that the station or network or any equipment designed,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1122 | constructed, installed, established, maintained or operated in accordance with any of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1123 | provisions of the Act, these Regulations or any condition of the licence, the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1124 | may impose a fee of $150 for the inspection.
@ref Rg 5 reg 66 (src:TA1999-RG5:1114-1124)
GIVEN `the licensee permits, or ensures permission for, an authorised officer who produces proof of identity to enter the place where the station or network is installed and to inspect, examine or test the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 66(1): the licence condition on inspection is met` MEANS
    `the licensee permits, or ensures permission for, an authorised officer who produces proof of identity to enter the place where the station or network is installed and to inspect, examine or test the equipment`

GIVEN `the owner or user asks the Authority to inspect the station or network for the second or subsequent time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 5 reg 66(2): the inspection fee in dollars the Authority may impose` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the owner or user asks the Authority to inspect the station or network for the second or subsequent time` THEN JUST 150
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1127 | 67. A licensee of a station or network shall permit an authorised officer or a police
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1128 | officer not below the rank of sergeant, upon production of proof of identity, to examine
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1129 | his licence, or if it is not immediately available, produce the licence at the office of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1130 | Authority or a police station named by the police officer within a reasonable period.
@ref Rg 5 reg 67 (src:TA1999-RG5:1127-1130)
GIVEN `the licensee permits an authorised officer or a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, on production of proof of identity, to examine the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `if the licence is not immediately available, it is produced within a reasonable period at the Authority's office or the police station named` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 67: the licensee has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the licensee permits an authorised officer or a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, on production of proof of identity, to examine the licence`
    AND `if the licence is not immediately available, it is produced within a reasonable period at the Authority's office or the police station named`

§ `Rg 5 regulation 68: secrecy`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1133 | 68. —(1) Except as may be provided by section 42 (2) of the Act, no person shall
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1134 | intercept or acquaint himself with the contents of any radio-communication other than
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1135 | those transmitted for general information or for the information of licensees belonging to
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1136 | the same licensed network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1137 | (2) Except as otherwise provided in these Regulations or by the conditions of a licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1138 | granted under these Regulations, every person having access to radio-communications
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1139 | shall hold strictly secret all radio-communications, other than those transmitted for
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1140 | general information, which may pass through his hands or come to his knowledge.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1141 | (3) Every person referred to in paragraph (2) shall not —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1142 | (a) directly or indirectly, disclose the contents of the radio-communications
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1143 | referred to in that paragraph except to a person entitled to become acquainted with
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1144 | the radio-communications or to an authorised officer or to a court; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1145 | (b) make any other use of such radio-communications.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1146 | (4) No person having unauthorised access to radio-communications shall print or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1147 | publish or cause to be printed or published in any newspaper, pamphlet, book or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1148 | document, any radio-communication that may pass through his hands or come to his
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1149 | knowledge, whether such radio-communication is for private or general reception.
@ref Rg 5 reg 68 (src:TA1999-RG5:1133-1149)
GIVEN `section 42(2) of the Act provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the radio-communication was transmitted for general information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was transmitted for the information of licensees belonging to the same licensed network, and the person is one of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 68(1): the person is prohibited from intercepting or acquainting himself with the contents of the radio-communication` MEANS
        (NOT `section 42(2) of the Act provides otherwise`)
    AND (NOT `the radio-communication was transmitted for general information`)
    AND (NOT `it was transmitted for the information of licensees belonging to the same licensed network, and the person is one of them`)

GIVEN `these Regulations or the conditions of a licence provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has access to radio-communications other than those transmitted for general information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person discloses the contents to a person entitled to them, an authorised officer or a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person discloses the contents to anyone else, or makes any other use of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 68(2) and (3): the person has breached the duty of secrecy` MEANS
        (NOT `these Regulations or the conditions of a licence provide otherwise`)
    AND `the person has access to radio-communications other than those transmitted for general information`
    AND `the person discloses the contents to anyone else, or makes any other use of them`
    AND (NOT `the person discloses the contents to a person entitled to them, an authorised officer or a court`)

GIVEN `the person has unauthorised access to the radio-communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person prints or publishes it, or causes it to be printed or published, in a newspaper, pamphlet, book or document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 68(4): the person has breached the prohibition on publishing` MEANS
    `the person has unauthorised access to the radio-communication` AND `the person prints or publishes it, or causes it to be printed or published, in a newspaper, pamphlet, book or document`

§ `Rg 5 regulations 69 and 70: lawful purposes and restrictions on transmission`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1152 | 69. No person shall operate or use any station or network for or in furtherance of any
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1153 | unlawful purpose.
@ref Rg 5 reg 69 (src:TA1999-RG5:1152-1153)
GIVEN `the person operates or uses the station or network for or in furtherance of an unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 69: the person has breached the regulation` MEANS
    `the person operates or uses the station or network for or in furtherance of an unlawful purpose`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1156 | 70. —(1) The transmission of superfluous signals by a station or network is prohibited.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1157 | (2) No test, trial or practical transmission shall be permitted except in such
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1158 | circumstances as to preclude the possibility of interference with any other station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1159 | network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1160 | (3) All tests, unless prior approval from the Authority has been obtained, shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1161 | conducted on dummy load.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1162 | (4) No person shall transmit —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1163 | (a) any message containing indecent, obscene or offensive language;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1164 | (b) any message for an improper or illegal purpose;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1165 | (c) any message which interferes with the operation of any authorised station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1166 | network; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1167 | (d) any message which, to his knowledge, is false or misleading and likely to
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1168 | prejudice the efficiency of any life-service or endanger the safety of any person or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1169 | of a place or premises, vessel, aircraft or vehicle.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1170 | (5) A licensee shall ensure that his station or network is worked in a manner which is
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1171 | safe and which does not impair or interfere with —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1172 | (a) any Armed Forces Communication; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1173 | (b) the efficient and convenient working or maintenance of any other station or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1174 | network, or telecommunication system or service in Singapore authorised by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1175 | Authority under the Act or these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1176 | (6) A licensee shall cease operating his station or network and shall take any other
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1177 | immediate action which the Authority stipulates as soon as the licensee observes, or when
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1178 | the licensee has been informed by the Authority or any other competent authority, that
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1179 | the working of the station or network causes interference to radio-communication.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1180 | (7) The licensee shall, where so directed by the Authority in writing, cease to operate all
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1181 | or any of the equipment comprised in his station for such period or periods of time as
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1182 | may be required by the Authority for the purposes of investigation of interference to
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1183 | radio-communications.
@ref Rg 5 reg 70 (src:TA1999-RG5:1156-1183)
GIVEN `the station or network transmits superfluous signals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 70(1): the transmission is prohibited` MEANS
    `the station or network transmits superfluous signals`

GIVEN `the test, trial or practical transmission can interfere with another station or network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority's prior approval was obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the test is conducted on dummy load` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 70(2) and (3): the test is permitted` MEANS
    (NOT `the test, trial or practical transmission can interfere with another station or network`)
    AND (`the Authority's prior approval was obtained` OR `the test is conducted on dummy load`)

GIVEN `the message contains indecent, obscene or offensive language` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message is for an improper or illegal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message interferes with the operation of any authorised station or network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message is, to the sender's knowledge, false or misleading and likely to prejudice the efficiency of any life-service or endanger safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 70(4): the person may transmit the message` MEANS
        (NOT `the message contains indecent, obscene or offensive language`)
    AND (NOT `the message is for an improper or illegal purpose`)
    AND (NOT `the message interferes with the operation of any authorised station or network`)
    AND (NOT `the message is, to the sender's knowledge, false or misleading and likely to prejudice the efficiency of any life-service or endanger safety`)

GIVEN `the station or network is worked safely` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it impairs or interferes with Armed Forces Communication, or the working or maintenance of any other authorised station, network, system or service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 70(5): the licensee is working the station or network as required` MEANS
    `the station or network is worked safely` AND (NOT `it impairs or interferes with Armed Forces Communication, or the working or maintenance of any other authorised station, network, system or service`)

GIVEN `the working of the station or network causes interference, as the licensee observes or the Authority or another competent authority informs the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee ceased operating and took the other immediate action the Authority stipulated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 70(6): the licensee has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the working of the station or network causes interference, as the licensee observes or the Authority or another competent authority informs the licensee`)
    OR `the licensee ceased operating and took the other immediate action the Authority stipulated`

GIVEN `the Authority directed the licensee in writing to cease operating equipment for the investigation of interference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee ceased to operate it for the period required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 70(7): the licensee has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority directed the licensee in writing to cease operating equipment for the investigation of interference`)
    OR `the licensee ceased to operate it for the period required`

§ `Rg 5 regulations 71 to 75: the Convention, interference, instructions and ad hoc assignment`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1185 | 71. —(1) The provisions of the International Telecommunication Convention and the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1186 | regulations for the time being in force thereunder shall, so far as they are applicable,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1187 | apply to any station or network established or operated in Singapore and to any message
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1188 | transmitted or received by such station or network.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1189 | (2) The Authority may, in its discretion, waive the application of any of the provisions
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1190 | or regulations referred to in paragraph (1) to any station, network or message.
@ref Rg 5 reg 71 (src:TA1999-RG5:1185-1190)
GIVEN `the provision is of the International Telecommunication Convention or the regulations in force under it, so far as applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority waived its application to the station, network or message` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 71: the provision applies to the station or network established or operated in Singapore, and to messages transmitted or received` MEANS
    `the provision is of the International Telecommunication Convention or the regulations in force under it, so far as applicable` AND (NOT `the Authority waived its application to the station, network or message`)

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1193 | 72. It is a condition of every licence that any owner or user of electrical, electronic or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1194 | radio-communication equipment under the licence causing or suspected of causing
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1195 | electrical or radiated interference or disturbance to telecommunication equipment,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1196 | stations, networks or systems belonging to or authorised or approved by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1197 | shall permit an authorised officer to inspect his equipment in order to determine whether
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1198 | the interference is in fact caused by the equipment.
@ref Rg 5 reg 72 (src:TA1999-RG5:1193-1198)
GIVEN `the equipment causes or is suspected of causing electrical or radiated interference or disturbance to equipment, stations, networks or systems belonging to or authorised or approved by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner or user permits an authorised officer to inspect the equipment to determine whether it causes the interference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 72: the licence condition is met` MEANS
    (NOT `the equipment causes or is suspected of causing electrical or radiated interference or disturbance to equipment, stations, networks or systems belonging to or authorised or approved by the Authority`)
    OR `the owner or user permits an authorised officer to inspect the equipment to determine whether it causes the interference`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1201 | 73. —(1) The Authority may, where requested by any person to —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1202 | (a) investigate, for the second or subsequent time, the cause of electrical or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1203 | radiated interference or disturbance to telecommunication equipment, stations,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1204 | networks or systems; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1205 | (b) measure and compute the field strength of radiated electromagnetic energy of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1206 | any electrical, electronic or radio-communication equipment,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1207 | charge a fee of $100 per hour or part thereof for work done.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1208 | (2) Where the Authority undertakes to measure and compute the field strength of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1209 | radiated electromagnetic energy under paragraph (1), the Authority shall determine the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1210 | measuring device to be used, the method by which and the conditions under which tests
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1211 | are to be conducted and the manner in which the field strength from readings afforded by
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1212 | the measuring device is computed.
@ref Rg 5 reg 73 (src:TA1999-RG5:1201-1212)
GIVEN `a person asks the Authority to investigate the cause of interference for the second or subsequent time, or to measure and compute the field strength of radiated energy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `hours or part of an hour of work` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 5 reg 73(1): the fee in dollars the Authority may charge` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a person asks the Authority to investigate the cause of interference for the second or subsequent time, or to measure and compute the field strength of radiated energy`
           THEN JUST (100 TIMES `hours or part of an hour of work`)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1215 | 74. —(1) Where the Authority determines that interference or disturbance to
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1216 | telecommunication equipment, stations, networks or systems is or may be caused by any
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1217 | particular electrical, electronic or radio-communication equipment, the Authority may, by
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1218 | notice in writing, direct the owner or user of that electrical, electronic or radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1219 | communication equipment to do, at his own expense, any one or more of the following:
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1220 | (a) take suitable measures to eliminate or reduce the interference or disturbance;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1221 | (b) remedy a fault in or the improper operation of the equipment;
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1222 | (c) modify or alter the equipment; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1223 | (d) disconnect the equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1224 | (2) The Authority may require any action required to be taken under paragraph (1) to be
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1225 | effected within such period of time as the Authority may determine having regard to the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1226 | circumstances of each case.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1227 | (3) In addition to any action the Authority may take under this regulation, the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1228 | may —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1229 | (a) by notice in writing, prohibit the installation or use of that electrical, electronic
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1230 | or radio-communication equipment unless and until the directions under
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1231 | paragraphs (1) and (2) are complied with; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1232 | (b) where it considers it necessary, seal or remove the equipment or any part
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1233 | thereof referred to in paragraph (1).
@ref Rg 5 reg 74 (src:TA1999-RG5:1215-1233)
GIVEN `the Authority determines that interference or disturbance to its equipment, stations, networks or systems is or may be caused by particular equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 74(1): the Authority may by written notice direct the owner or user, at the owner's or user's expense, to take suitable measures, remedy a fault, modify or alter the equipment, or disconnect it` MEANS
    `the Authority determines that interference or disturbance to its equipment, stations, networks or systems is or may be caused by particular equipment`

GIVEN `the Authority gave notice in writing prohibiting the installation or use unless and until the directions are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directions have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 74(3)(a): the person may install or use the equipment` MEANS
    (NOT `the Authority gave notice in writing prohibiting the installation or use unless and until the directions are complied with`) OR `the directions have been complied with`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1236 | 75. —(1) The Authority may permit any person to use any radio frequency band in
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1237 | respect of any network or station for a period not exceeding 90 days at a time upon
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1238 | payment of the fees specified in Part V of the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1239 | (2) Paragraph (1) shall not apply to any use of radio frequency band granted under a
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1240 | spectrum right, or permitted under a station (spectrum) licence, a network (spectrum)
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1241 | licence, a station licence, a network licence or a class licence.
@ref Rg 5 reg 75 (src:TA1999-RG5:1236-1241)
GIVEN `the use is granted under a spectrum right or permitted under a station (spectrum) licence, network (spectrum) licence, station licence, network licence or class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days of use at a time` IS A NUMBER
      `the fees in Part V of the First Schedule are paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 75: the Authority may permit the person to use the radio frequency band on an ad hoc temporary basis` MEANS
    (NOT `the use is granted under a spectrum right or permitted under a station (spectrum) licence, network (spectrum) licence, station licence, network licence or class licence`)
    AND (`days of use at a time` AT MOST 90)
    AND `the fees in Part V of the First Schedule are paid`

§ `Rg 5 regulations 76, 77, 79 and 80: miscellaneous`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1247 | 76. No approval, consent, licence or authorisation given by the Authority pursuant to
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1248 | these Regulations shall be taken as specifically authorising or approving any act or thing
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1249 | for the purposes of the Code of Practice for Competition in the provision of
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1250 | Telecommunication Services 2000 (G.N. No. S 412/2000) issued by the Authority under
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1251 | section 26 of the Act.
@ref Rg 5 reg 76 (src:TA1999-RG5:1247-1251)
GIVEN `the act or thing was approved under these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 76: the approval specifically authorises the act for the purposes of the Code of Practice for Competition in the provision of Telecommunication Services 2000` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1254 | 77. —(1) If the Authority is satisfied that any licence issued by it is lost, destroyed or
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1255 | defaced, the Authority may, upon payment of a fee of $10, issue a replacement licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1256 | (2) No replacement licence shall be issued in place of a defaced licence unless the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1257 | defaced licence is surrendered to the Authority for cancellation.
@ref Rg 5 reg 77 (src:TA1999-RG5:1254-1257)
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied the licence is lost, destroyed or defaced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence is defaced and is surrendered to the Authority for cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence is defaced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 5 reg 77: the fee in dollars for a replacement licence the Authority may issue` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the Authority is satisfied the licence is lost, destroyed or defaced` THEN NOTHING
           IF `the licence is defaced` AND (NOT `the licence is defaced and is surrendered to the Authority for cancellation`) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST 10

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1268 | 79. The Minister or the Authority (subject to the directions of the Minister) may waive
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1269 | the application of all or any of the provisions of these Regulations, any or all of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1270 | conditions in any licence and any fee payable under these Regulations.
@ref Rg 5 reg 79 (src:TA1999-RG5:1268-1270)
GIVEN `the Minister, or the Authority subject to the Minister's directions, waives the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 79: the Regulation, licence condition or fee does not apply` MEANS
    `the Minister, or the Authority subject to the Minister's directions, waives the application`

-- src:TA1999-RG5:1273 | 80. Notwithstanding the revocation of the Radio-communication Regulations (Rg 3,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1274 | 1999 Ed.) the holder of any licence in respect of any network or station granted in
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1275 | accordance with the revoked Regulations may —
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1276 | (a) until the expiry of the licence or unless the licence is cancelled or suspended in
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1277 | accordance with the Act; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1278 | (b) subject to the provisions of the revoked Regulations,
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1279 | perform all the acts for which the licence was granted as if these Regulations had not
-- src:TA1999-RG5:1280 | been enacted.
@ref Rg 5 reg 80 (src:TA1999-RG5:1273-1280)
GIVEN `the person holds a licence for a network or station granted under the revoked Radio-communication Regulations (Rg 3, 1999 Ed.)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence has not expired and has not been cancelled or suspended under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 80: the holder may perform all the acts for which the licence was granted, subject to the revoked Regulations` MEANS
    `the person holds a licence for a network or station granted under the revoked Radio-communication Regulations (Rg 3, 1999 Ed.)` AND `the licence has not expired and has not been cancelled or suspended under the Act`
